WEBVTT

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:36.560
Sylvette? You have grown up...

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.900
Suede, is that you?

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:42.870
Gauche?

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:47.690
Lag... Lag Seeing, yes?

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:51.420
I missed you.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.320
Gauche!

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:03.510
Welcome Home

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.430
Please, Master!

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:10.070
I want Gauche to live together 
with Sylvette as soon as possible!

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:11.750
And so...?

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.720
Why are you looking at me?

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:17.440
Well, isn't this something that 
needs the Doctor's approval?

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.210
Doctor Thunderland, please!

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:23.350
Doctor?

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:25.360
Seeing...

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.770
I understand how you must feel.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:32.830
But Suede has just regained consciousness. 
He still needs time to recuperate.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:34.720
Right...

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:40.830
Plus, I haven't confirmed whether or not 
Suede's lost heart has really returned.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.580
That's not true!

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:46.200
My letter bullet is bringing 
Gauche's heart back!

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:48.550
If you put in too much, 
you will lose your heart.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.100
You will lose everything.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:54.980
You will cause grief to the 
people precious to you.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:58.490
That's the strong, kind person I know!

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:07.280
So, please! Sylvette's been waiting for the 
day they can live in their house together again!

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:12.760
I wonder where I'll have Lag and Niche 
sleep after my brother comes back?

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.170
Listen, Seeing...

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:20.020
If what you say is true, and Suede 
is getting his real heart back,

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:23.480
that's all the more reason 
not to release him.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:28.240
I have a great number of 
tests I need to run on him.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.480
Also...

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:35.530
I'm holding back while his 
memories are still jumbled up,

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:39.650
but I have a mountain of things 
I need to ask him about.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.870
Things you need to ask?

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:48.580
Yes. Like why he aided the 
anti-Amberground-government organization, Reverse.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:55.480
Fundamentally, I need to determine whether 
he robbed letters of his own free will...

00:03:55.950 --> 00:04:01.170
H-He was just being used by 
Reverse after he lost his heart!

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:05.140
...I think...

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:10.560
Then what do you think happened in Akatsuki 
five years ago that caused him to lose his heart?

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.840
I'm sure you want to know as well, young man.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:16.560
Yes...

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:21.280
That's the reason why Gauche must 
remain here in the Bee Hive.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:23.640
I see...

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.220
Yes, that's the reason.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.070
I hope there are no hard feelings, Seeing.

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:28.950
However...

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.530
Tonight I'll make an exception.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.710
He may return home.

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:38.320
M-Master!

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.440
What's the big deal if it's just for a day?

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:45.880
And there's a possibility that returning home 
will cause his memories to return more quickly.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.640
Yes, that's a possibility...

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:50.400
Really?

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.160
Yeah.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:55.520
The Maka girl and Aria-kun should be 
returning from their delivery today.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.520
You're gonna throw a big party, right?

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.810
Right!

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:06.250
Thank you, Master!

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:08.620
I'll go tell Gauche!

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.180
Just for tonight, okay?

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.210
Right!

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.200
Trying to be the understanding boss?

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.920
You have a problem with that?

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:29.460
Gauche!

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:31.770
Lag Seeing...

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:36.510
What is the matter? Why the rush?

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.990
The Master said it was okay for 
you to go home, just for tonight!

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:43.060
Gauche?

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.940
Let's go and make Sylvette really happy!

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:49.700
Yes...

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.850
I'll come pick you up later, okay?

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:54.950
I have to go out on a delivery now.

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:56.380
You do?

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:58.380
It's just out somewhere nearby.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.830
I think I'll be back by the 18th bell.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:03.590
In that case...

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:08.220
...I will accompany you on this delivery.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:17.680
G-Going out on delivery 
together with Gauche...

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:18.820
How should I...

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:23.560
Is something the matter?

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.320
N-No, it's nothing...

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:34.630
Oh, if it ain't the little Bee boy!

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:36.970
Pissarro-san...

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:40.150
Not together with your Fairy dingo?

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:46.680
Today, I am his dingo.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:50.710
So the fairy's on vacation, eh?

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:52.760
Boy?

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:57.660
Gauche is my dingo...

00:06:58.470 --> 00:06:59.610
Lag Seeing?

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:02.140
Is that a problem?

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:04.010
Not at all!

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:05.870
That's right...

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:07.910
I'm finally together alone with Gauche...

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:12.320
I have to show him how wonderful 
a Letter Bee I've become!

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:14.070
Lag Seeing?

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:19.770
All right, Gauche. Today you can 
come along with me as my dingo.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:20.500
Right.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:09.180
Ah, Lag Seeing...

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:10.020
What is it?

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:13.350
Is it acceptable for you not to get 
the signature of the recipient?

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:20.970
Excuse me!

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:23.410
Please sign here!

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:30.580
What is the matter?

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:33.550
You seem depressed.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:36.470
Yeah...

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:41.170
Is it because I came along on your delivery?

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.710
T-That's not...

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:48.630
...why... exactly...

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:58.770
I wanted to show you how wonderful 
a Letter Bee I was, Gauche...

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:00.890
But all I did was...

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:05.620
Do not worry.

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:14.150
The fact that you have become a wonderful 
Letter Bee has already been delivered to my heart.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:21.250
Because it was you who 
returned my lost heart to me.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.250
Gauche...

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.380
I remember...

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:46.060
You mean, about the time you delivered me?

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:46.840
Yes.

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:51.250
But that was near the Jose desert.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:52.840
This is nowhere near...

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:54.380
The fluff of the chippa flower.

00:09:57.920 --> 00:09:59.070
Wasn't it?

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:01.450
Yeah!

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:12.300
Lag Seeing...

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:15.960
I have something I must say to you.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:17.090
What?

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:21.680
I did not keep my promise to you.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.410
Your promise?

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:28.480
I promised to look into your 
mother when I got to Akatsuki.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:30.410
You remembered that?

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:31.890
Yes...

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:40.730
I am sorry.

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:51.830
Did Gauche come with me on my delivery 
so he could apologize for that?

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.220
What is the matter?

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:11.580
Gauche...

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:14.400
Gauche!

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:21.430
You're back... For real...

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:25.290
The Gauche Suede I know is really back!

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:31.290
Gauche!

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.560
Gauche...

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:03.490
Do I have something on my face?

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:06.370
Oh, no...

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:13.220
It's just you and I are coming home together 
with Sylvette waiting for us... It's like a dream!

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.230
Gauche, let's hurry!

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:22.550
H-Hey! Lag Seeing...

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:30.120
We're home!

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:32.850
Lag! Niche has also returned!

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:36.100
I promised, as your dingo!

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:40.750
Brother...

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:48.170
Sylvette...

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:54.130
Welcome home, Brother.

00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:58.930
I am home, Sylvette.

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:07.050
Welcome home, Brother!

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:14.600
Thank goodness...

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:17.560
I'm so happy...

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:22.810
Thank you, Lag.

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:26.460
I'm so glad I put my trust in you.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:31.800
To be able to say "Welcome home" 
to my brother once again...

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:34.000
Sylvette...

00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:36.020
Thank you...

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:40.710
Thank you... so much!

00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:50.360
Do both Lag and Sylvette hurt?

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:51.630
No, that's not it.

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:03.860
Oh? Both of you?

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.080
Yeah.

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:06.800
We went on a delivery.

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:07.850
That's no fair!

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:11.970
You hogged him all to yourself, Lag!

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:14.060
No wonder you seemed so happy.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.140
Huh? But that's not...

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:19.290
...actually it is.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:26.760
Largo-san should have at 
least given you the day off.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.940
That's not true, Sylvette.

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:35.600
For people who live apart from each other, 
the letters they write are their very hearts.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.350
As long as there are people waiting 
on tiptoes for those letters,

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:40.690
I can't take a day off so easily.

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:44.970
That's the kind of job being a Letter Bee is.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:47.940
You sound like my brother.

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:52.970
He comes back, and you turn into him!

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:53.620
Sheesh...

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:57.640
Now that I think about it, that's 
something you taught me, Gauche.

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:01.800
But now, surely you have 
adopted it as your own belief.

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:04.480
Yeah, Gauche!

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:07.210
Gauche is Lag's happiness.

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:10.490
I see, happiness!

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:17.510
Here!

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:21.980
My special soup! Your favorite.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:23.690
Thanks for the food!

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:24.860
I've got plenty for seconds.

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:27.530
R-Right...

00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:30.510
Thank you.

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:39.090
So pukey...

00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:45.390
I don't want to be mean to Sylvette, but 
only Gauche could eat this and say, "Delicious".

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.140
But...

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:57.320
I feel sorry for that person you hold dear.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:02.940
His heart became some of the light 
that was scattered upon the world.

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:09.370
It's already beyond the point where it 
can be gathered and returned to him.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:20.220
How many years has it been since 
my heart has felt this warmth?

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:26.280
It is delicious.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:28.540
You are a gifted cook, Sylvette.

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:51.720
Sylvette, can I have more?

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:53.840
Sure, Brother...

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:56.070
Me, too!

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:57.430
Really, Lag?

00:16:57.430 --> 00:16:59.830
How about you, Aria-san?

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.570
Me? I'm...

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:14.980
Goodnight, Gauche.

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:22.080
Thank you for the meal.

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:24.550
Goodnight, Aria-san.

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:35.660
Doctor... What brings you this late?

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:37.940
I forgot to tell you something.

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:46.370
Right now, Suede should have recovered 
the memories that Lag had access to.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:53.130
But if he is still Noir, he could probably 
pull off a deception of this order.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:06.510
Brother, it's morning!

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:08.210
Brother!

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:10.160
I'll go wake him up.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:11.130
Please.

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:15.040
Gauche, good morning.

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:21.420
He already left?

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:24.580
Lag?

00:18:40.190 --> 00:18:41.300
Lawrence.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:48.310
According to reports from the Bee Hive, it 
sounds like Noir has regained Gauche Suede's heart.

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:49.640
His heart?

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:55.720
If that's true, then we can't 
use him as a Marauder any more.

00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:59.270
I'm gettin' hooked on these sour things!

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:03.420
It will be a problem if he says too much.

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:05.200
Get rid of him.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:07.580
Understood.

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:46.730
Next: Roda Wanders
